4.5. Database Relationships
4.5.1. Digital Twin Hierarchy Relationships
SITE → ROOM (1:N)
- Foreign Key: room.site_id references site.site_id.
- On Delete Action: RESTRICT (Prevents deletion of a site if active rooms are linked to it).
- Description: Represents physical spatial hierarchy where a data center site contains multiple rooms.
ROOM → RACK (1:N)
- Foreign Key: rack.room_id references room.room_id.
- On Delete Action: RESTRICT.
- Description: A server room houses multiple equipment server racks.
RACK → SERVER (1:N)
- Foreign Key: server.rack_id references rack.rack_id.
- On Delete Action: RESTRICT.
- Description: Represents vertical rack unit mounting where one rack contains multiple physical/virtual servers.
SERVER → CONTAINER (1:N)
- Foreign Key: container.server_id references server.server_id.
- On Delete Action: CASCADE (Deleting a server removes its hosted container metadata).
- Description: Tracks Docker containers and virtualized workloads hosted on a server.
4.5.2. Asset Identification and Warranty Relationships
SERVER → MARKER (1:1)
- Foreign Key: marker.server_id references server.server_id (UNIQUE constraint).
- On Delete Action: CASCADE.
- Description: Binds exactly one physical QR or ArUco visual marker to a server for AR scanning identification.
SERVER → WARRANTY (1:1)
- Foreign Key: warranty.server_id references server.server_id (UNIQUE constraint).
- On Delete Action: CASCADE.
- Description: Associates a server with its hardware warranty provider and service period details.
4.5.3. Real-Time Telemetry and Monitoring Relationships
SERVER → TELEMETRY (1:N)
- Foreign Key: telemetry.server_id references server.server_id.
- On Delete Action: CASCADE.
- Description: Captures high-frequency time-series resource usage metrics generated by the Collector Agent every 5 seconds.
SERVER → ALERT (1:N)
- Foreign Key: alert.server_id references server.server_id.
- On Delete Action: CASCADE.
- Description: Links system threshold breach events (CPU, RAM, Disk) back to the offending server.
4.5.4. Incident Management and Maintenance Workflow Relationships
ALERT → INCIDENT (1:1)
- Foreign Key: incident.alert_id references alert.alert_id (UNIQUE constraint).
- On Delete Action: SET NULL.
- Description: Escalates severe performance alerts into formal system incidents requiring technician intervention.
INCIDENT → TICKET (1:1)
- Foreign Key: ticket.incident_id references incident.incident_id (UNIQUE constraint).
- On Delete Action: RESTRICT.
- Description: Creates an actionable work ticket for an identified incident.
TICKET → MAINTENANCE (1:N)
- Foreign Key: maintenance.ticket_id references ticket.ticket_id.
- On Delete Action: CASCADE.
- Description: Logs step-by-step physical repair logs and actions performed by field technicians.
4.5.5. Access Control and Audit Logging Relationships
ROLE → USER (1:N)
- Foreign Key: user.role_id references role.role_id.
- On Delete Action: RESTRICT.
- Description: Enforces Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) across system users.
USER → TICKET (1:N)
- Foreign Keys:
+ ticket.assigned_to references user.user_id.
+ ticket.created_by references user.user_id.
- On Delete Action: SET NULL.
- Description: Tracks ticket creation by operators and field assignment to technicians.
USER → AUDIT_LOG (1:N)
- Foreign Key: audit_log.user_id references user.user_id.
- On Delete Action: SET NULL.
- Description: Records user activity logs for security auditing and accountability.

